<figure id="S5.SS2.fig3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.F3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_middle" style="width:246.4pt;"><img src="2510.00635v1/Images/nsfw.png" id="S5.SS2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:340/365;" width="340" height="365" alt="Refer to caption">
<br class="ltx_break ltx_break">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Visual comparison of <span id="S5.F3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nudity</span> and <span id="S5.F3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">violence</span> across attack methods under different erasure strategies. <span id="S5.F3.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFF00;">Yellow</span> framed images are original generations from Flux.1 [dev]. <span id="S5.F3.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Blue</span> bars and blurring are added for publication purposes. Our method achieves precise concept reactivation while preserving the layout and unrelated elements of the images.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.F4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_middle" style="width:141.1pt;"><img src="2510.00635v1/Images/category.png" id="S5.SS2.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:195/362;" width="195" height="362" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Visual results on <span id="S5.F4.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Entity</span>, <span id="S5.F4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Abstraction</span>, and <span id="S5.F4.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Relationship</span>. The leftmost column shows the defense effect of EA. <span id="S5.F4.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFF00;">Yellow</span> framed images denote the original generations from Flux.1 [dev].</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation on miscellaneousness.</span>
We evaluate our method on 3 broader categories: <span id="S5.SS2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Entity</span>, <span id="S5.SS2.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Abstraction</span> and <span id="S5.SS2.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Relationship</span>. Here, we choose 10 concepts for each category (see Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Baselines and Implementation Details ‣ Erased, But Not Forgotten: Erased Rectified Flow Transformers Still Remain Unsafe Under Concept Attack" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a> for full list of concepts) and adopt CLIP classification as the measuring metrics.
As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 5.2 Results ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Erased, But Not Forgotten: Erased Rectified Flow Transformers Still Remain Unsafe Under Concept Attack" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, our attack consistently outperforms baselines, with stronger gains on abstract and relational concepts, confirming its stable effectiveness across both concrete and abstract categories.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.SS2.fig6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.T4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_middle" style="width:230.5pt;">
<br class="ltx_break ltx_break">
<table id="S5.T4.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_figure_panel ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T4.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T4.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Category</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;" colspan="2"><span id="S5.T4.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Entity</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;" colspan="2"><span id="S5.T4.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Abstract</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;" colspan="2"><span id="S5.T4.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Relation</span></th></tr>
